 "strategy": {
  "summary": "Trade the INTRADAY spread between ES and NQ, flat by the close every day (no overnight holds). Each leg is measured from that day's open, so the spread starts at 0 each session; when ES runs ahead of or behind \u03b2 \u00d7 NQ by an unusual amount, bet on the gap closing before the close. \u03b2 comes from Ning & Lee (Purdue Statistics, 2024): the ratio whose spread reverts fastest (the empirical mean-reversion time, EMRT), fit monthly on these intraday spreads. The OLS slope and 1:1 run alongside as controls. Designed after v1, whose flat-at-close versions all failed because its multi-day spread rarely reverted within the day.",
  "formula": "spread = (ES \u2212 today's ES open) \u00f7 open \u2212 \u03b2 \u00d7 (NQ \u2212 today's NQ open) \u00f7 open; \u03b2 = argmin EMRT",
  "rules": [
   {
    "label": "Hedge",
    "text": "At each month start, fit \u03b2 on the previous 1, 3 or 6 months only. EMRT: mark every swing of at least C \u00d7 the spread's sd (an 'important extremum'), time how long each takes to get back to the mean within the same session (a swing still open at the close counts until the close), and pick the \u03b2 from 0.20 to 3.00 with the shortest average (C = 1.5 or 2.0), as long as the spread's variance is at most 2\u00d7 the OLS spread's. Controls: OLS slope; \u03b2 = 1."
   },
   {
    "label": "Enter",
    "text": "z = the spread against the formation window's mean and sd, or by time of day: against the same bar of the last 20 or 60 sessions. A fresh cross below \u2212entry buys the spread (long ES, short \u03b2 \u00d7 NQ); above +entry sells it. Both legs fill at the next bar's open. Optionally no entries in the first 30 minutes; none in the last 30; a signal while a position is open is dropped."
   },
   {
    "label": "Exit",
    "text": "Close when z gets back to 0 (at mean) or half-way to it; optional stop once z runs a further 1.5 past the entry level; optional time stop after 3 \u00d7 the spread's EMRT. Anything still open is closed at the session's last close: never held overnight."
   },
   {
    "label": "Size",
    "text": "Both / long spread / short spread; one position at a time. Whole ES and NQ contracts, the two legs' full contract value together no more than the account (no leverage), starting from $10,000,000 so the ratio is carried by tens of contracts."
   }
  ],
